## 0. Abstract

This project looks at whether recent search performance can be used to prioritise content pages for refresh review. I used page-level data from the FlyRank ML Internship warehouse and created monthly observations so that recent performance could be compared with what happened in the following month. 
I compared a simple trend-based baseline with logistic regression and Random Forest using a time-based test period. The Random Forest performed best at the top of the ranking, with a Precision@50 of 78% compared with a 69.2% decline rate in the test set, although its ROC AUC was only 0.571. 
The final output is a ranked review queue with reason codes that can help editors decide which pages may be worth checking first.

